From 224bc8ddfe1bfabe0e51f5fe8b4870d5577f9044 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:43:03 +0000
Subject: software_isp: Gather the statistics on the corrected image

The statistics are taken from the raw frame, before the GPU debayer
applies lens shading correction, which lifts the image corners two to
three times on a phone module. Exposure then judges bright areas near
the edges at a fraction of the level they come out at, and lets them
clip: a white table across half of the frame read as mid grey.

Apply the frame's lens shading gains above the black level to each
sample in the statistics, as the debayer does, when the GPU debayer
applies them. The gains are interpolated once per sampled line; the
CPU debayer does not apply lens shading, so its statistics stay as
they were.

The GPU debayer outputs a window of the input, centred when the output
is smaller, but set the statistics window to that window's size at the
origin, as the CPU debayer does. The CPU debayer hands the statistics
only the lines it processes; the GPU debayer hands them the whole input
buffer (SwStatsCpu::processFrame()), which then starts from the
window's x and y. The statistics described the top left corner of the
input: with a 1920x1080 output of a 4080x3072 sensor, a region that
barely overlaps the image, so exposure brightened a scene whose top
left corner was dark until what was shown clipped.

Pass the window itself, as for quad Bayer input already.

The GPU debayer scales the whole input to the output, cropping only
quad Bayer input to the output's aspect ratio, but for ordinary Bayer
input set the statistics window to a centred window of the output's
size in the input: with a 1920x1080 output of a 4080x3072 sensor, the
middle 47% x 35% of the image. Exposure and white balance then went
by the centre alone: a lamp in the middle of a room darkened the whole
frame, and the next frame, a little to its side, came out twice as
bright.

Take the whole input as the window for ordinary Bayer input, the part
of it that is output.

Fixes: 59db91b13 ("libcamera: software_isp: debayer_egl: Gather statistics on the output window")

Signed-off-by: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
